This repository ships two different things, licensed differently.

The code — the TypeScript source, compiled output, type definitions,
scoring engine, validation, localization logic, and JSON Schema,
everything that makes psytools run — is licensed under the MIT
License below. Copyright (c) 2026 Samed Kahyaoglu.

The bundled instrument text — the titles, descriptions, instructions,
item wording, and answer-option labels of the seventeen third-party
psychological assessment instruments psytools ships, in every
language psytools provides them — is licensed by each instrument's
own rights holder, on the terms recorded instrument by instrument in
SOURCES.md. SOURCES.md, not the MIT License below, is where your
rights over any specific instrument's text come from.

Most bundled instruments are free to use, including in commercial
products. Some carry conditions of their own — mandatory attribution,
or other limits on what "free" covers. Three of them, the ECR-R, the
ERQ, and the HSPS, are licensed for non-commercial research only.
Read SOURCES.md before you rely on any instrument's text, particularly
before commercial use.

The MIT License below is the license for the code. The bundled
instrument text is licensed as described above, not under this MIT
grant.


